# OGGI Wholesale v2 — real HTTP security headers
#
# Hosting is Cloudflare Workers (per Hadi's explicit instruction --
# "don't do Pages, do Workers"), NOT Cloudflare Pages. This file is kept
# because Cloudflare's Workers static-assets server natively honors a
# _headers file in the assets directory using the exact same format
# Pages used -- it is not a Pages-only mechanism. worker.js's fetch
# handler (see its header comment) is the authoritative source for this
# policy and sets these same headers explicitly on every response via
# `run_worker_first = true` in wrangler.toml; this file is a second,
# native layer of defense in case that ever changes. Keep both in sync
# by hand if the policy changes (see docs/BATCH-14-DEPLOY-RECORD.md and
# docs/BATCH-14-SCHEMA-MIGRATION-RECORD.md).
#
# Policy rationale (script-src strict, style-src needs 'unsafe-inline'
# for this build's extensive inline style="..." attributes, img-src open
# to any https host since wholesalers set arbitrary product photo URLs)
# is documented in full in worker.js's header comment -- this is the
# same policy, just in the native _headers file format.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' https: data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://olaipgdckbgjediddloj.supabase.co wss://olaipgdckbgjediddloj.supabase.co; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()
